  "decision": "An item is GO when (a) on the thinned rows, pooled over July and December, its thinned-input RMSE is below ref32's thinned-input RMSE and the paired-day 95% interval of the difference (days of both months) lies below zero; (b) on thinned inputs its whole non-LIRF RMSE is below ref32's in July and in December; and (c) its October R2 at b = 0.5 is at most 0.02 points above ref32's (the cost on natural 2025 coverage stays small). Of several GO items the one with the lowest pooled thinned-row RMSE is carried forward. A GO goes to a separately declared development round (the item as a network member or a replacement; its rule adds the thinned-regime reading to the usual January / July / December reading; hardware named then); every upload is the user's decision. Without a GO the positional-drift question is closed for falling coverage, with the penalties on record. Coverage that rose (EGLL, EDDM, LEMD in July 2026) cannot be simulated by removal and is not covered by this batch.",
